Usage: ruralz bundle export FORMAT [DIR] [FLAGS]

OpenAPI 3.x, Postman collection or DOT graph of a Bundle.

Exports one Environment's rendered Bundle: openapi writes an OpenAPI 3.1
document of its HTTP Routes as YAML, or with --output json as JSON; postman a
Postman collection v2.1 of the same operations; dot a Graphviz DOT graph of its
Routes, Policies and Upstreams, or with --route of one Route. A Route or method
without an OpenAPI operation is left out with a warning on standard error.
Exits 1 when the Bundle is invalid.

Arguments:
  FORMAT  Document format (openapi, postman or dot)
  DIR     Bundle directory or one-file Bundle (default .)

Flags:
  --env NAME           Render with this Environment's overlay and variables, read from --environments
  --environments FILE  Local Environment resources
  --help               Print this help
  --output yaml|json   Format of export openapi; postman always writes JSON and dot DOT text (yaml or json, default yaml)
  --output-file PATH   Write the document to PATH instead of standard output
  --route NAME         The Route of export dot
